</code_cell>

### Step 2: Read and write through each backend

The read and write commands differ in shape because the backends differ in kind. KV stores opaque values; database and cloud generate credentials on read.

```bash
# KV — write a static secret
vault kv put secret/cloud-iam/static access_key=AKIA... secret_key=wJalr... region=us-east-1
# KV — read it back
vault kv get -field=secret_key secret/cloud-iam/static

# Database — generate a credential (write once, read many)
vault read db/creds/app
# Cloud — generate a credential
vault read aws/creds/ci-role
```

A KV read returns the stored value. A database or cloud read returns a newly generated credential pair with a lease ID attached.

<code_cell>
